  "reasoning": "The defendant organized and led villagers via mass text messages to gather at a construction site and physically block the work by climbing a tower crane, causing the project to be halted for months and resulting in significant economic loss and social impact. This conduct constitutes a coordinated group action that disrupts the normal operation of a public place (the construction site) and public order. Under Chinese criminal law, such behavior fits the crime of ‘聚众扰乱公共场所秩序’ (Article 293). No other offenses (e.g., illegal possession of weapons, fraud, etc.) are supported by the facts.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]聚众扰乱公共场所秩序<eoa>"
}
